From 6d5471370b80d1b693a064e08f3f47a1bd247b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:33:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 45/48] test: add a fuzz target for OP_CHECKMLDSA44

The target builds a P2MR spend of a leaf <pk[0]> <pk[1]> <pk[2]>
OP_CHECKMLDSA44 with chunk sizes, stack depth, hash type, leaf version,
leaf depth and flags from the input, mostly well formed so that the
later rules are reached, and compares the script error with the one a
separate model of the rules, in their order, predicts. Only the
ML-DSA-44 verification itself is replaced, by a result the input picks;
splitting off the hash type and computing the signature message run as
in consensus. It also requires a DeferringSignatureChecker to give the
same result and error.
---
 src/test/fuzz/CMakeLists.txt   |   1 +
 src/test/fuzz/p2mr_mldsa44.cpp | 167 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 168 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/test/fuzz/p2mr_mldsa44.cpp

